docs {
  # POST /api/artworks/artworks/:slug/buy/ — Reserve an artwork + start Stripe Checkout

  Reserves an artwork (`available → reserved`), creates an `ArtworkOrder`
  (`pending_payment`) and a `mode=payment` Checkout Session (30-min expiry).
  Returns `{checkout_url}` — redirect the buyer there (full page).
  Public endpoint, no `Authorization` header. Throttled: `artwork_buys`
  20/hour per client (`429` when exceeded — wait and retry).

  Replace `obra-ejemplo` with a real artwork slug (slugs are human-readable,
  e.g. `la-columna-rota`). Only `available` artworks can be bought — check
  the catalog `status` first (`reserved` → "sale in progress",
  `sold` → "sold", no button).

  Same email + live session → same URL (`200`, follow it either way).
  Different email while reserved → `409`.

  ## Status codes

  - `201 Created` — new reservation, `{checkout_url}` ready
  - `200 OK` — same buyer re-clicked while their session is live, same `{checkout_url}`
  - `400 Bad Request` — bad currency/email (`data` has field errors)
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown slug or inactive artwork
  - `409 Conflict` — reserved by another buyer, or artwork not `available`
  - `502 Bad Gateway` — Stripe did not respond (nothing reserved, retry later)
  - `503 Service Unavailable` — backend misconfigured (`PUBLIC_SITE_URL`)
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — throttled (20 buys/hour)

  ## Request

  ```json
  {
    "currency": "mxn",
    "email": "comprador@example.com"
  }
  ```

  `currency` is `mxn` or `usd`. `email` is the buyer email (backend
  lowercases it; it is locked as Stripe `customer_email`).

  ## Response (201/200)

  ```json
  {
    "checkout_url": "https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/cs_test_123"
  }
  ```

  ## Error (400/404/409/502/503/429)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Reserva en curso para esta obra.",
    "data": {}
  }
  ```

  - `400` → `message: "Invalid data"`, `data` carries per-field errors
  - `409` → `message: "Reserva en curso para esta obra."` (another buyer)
    or `"Obra no disponible."` (not `available`)
  - `502` → `message: "Stripe no respondió."`
  - `503` → `message: "Ventas no configuradas (PUBLIC_SITE_URL)."`
}
